# Decision-Maker GPU assignment (single source of truth — EDIT THIS for your box).
#
# This repo supports split GPU roles: the SERVICE (live /v1/decisionmaker answers)
# and TRAINING (fine-tune + calibration) may run on different physical GPUs.
# Each value is an NVIDIA device UUID as reported by `nvidia-smi --query-gpu=uuid`
# (or `scripts/verify_gpu.sh` in this repo). The container runtime injects the
# right one into the right role; the engine maps it to CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES before
# torch loads. See README.md §"GPU assignment" and deploy/ for the wiring.

# GPU that runs the live decision service (any role that must stay responsive).
DECISIONMAKER_SERVE_GPU_DEVICES=GPU-58e5f98d-a4f4-4cff-a9fc-16df0667d2fd

# GPU used for fine-tuning / calibration runs (larger card recommended).
DECISIONMAKER_TRAIN_GPU_DEVICES=GPU-34466eba-2642-c31a-2e44-6451b6a6b425